    "https://jobs.wgu.edu/academic-careers": {
      "title": "Academic Careers",
      "description": "Academic & Faculty Careers | WGU Skip to content Jobs Search\n                All Jobs Academic\n                Careers Staff\n                & Corporate Careers Tech\n                Careers Schools School\n                of Technology School\n                of Business School\n                of Health School\n                of Education Life at WGU Life\n                at WGU Where\n                We Work Total\n                Rewards Search all jobs Close Site Navigation Careers Home Jobs Search All Jobs Academic Careers Staff & Corporate Careers Tech Careers Affiliates Schools School of Technology School of Business School of Health School of Education Life at WGU Where We Work Total Rewards How We Hire Talent Community (opens in new tab) Search all jobs Academic Careers Educate. Motivate. Transform. Academic careers at WGU focus on supporting learners through mentorship, instruction, and meaningful assessment.\n        As a faculty member or academic leader, you’ll help learners build real-world skills, stay on track, and move\n        confidently toward their goals. Find a Teaching Role That Matches Your Passion for Education Academic Career Paths Faculty Faculty roles at WGU are about making a direct, meaningful difference in learners' lives. You'll serve\n                  as a Mentor, Instructor, or Evaluator, providing personalized support, coaching, and instruction that\n                  helps learners progress with confidence in a flexible, competency-based environment. Accreditation & Compliance Accreditation and Compliance roles support the foundation that makes everything else possible. You'll\n                  help ensure academic quality, integrity, and trust—working behind the scenes to meet regulatory\n                  standards while enabling innovation and a continuous improvement model. Academic Strategy Academic Strategy roles are ideal for big-picture thinkers who enjoy turning insight into action.\n                  You'll work at the intersection of data, innovation, and academic excellence—helping WGU design,\n                  launch, and evolve programs that meet the needs of today's learners and tomorrow's workforce. Academic Leadership Academic Leadership roles are for those who want to lead with purpose and shape the future of\n                  education. In this area, you'll guide academic teams, influence strategy, and help scale innovative\n                  learning models that expand access and improve learner outcomes. Program Development & Learning Design Program Development and Learning Design roles are for creators and problem-solvers who want to build\n                  impactful learning experiences. In this area, you'll collaborate with academic and industry partners\n                  to design modern, engaging programs that prepare learners for real-world success. Program Mentor Our Program Mentors are the heart of our student success model at WGU. As a Program Mentor, you'll have the\n          unique opportunity to provide personalized, one-on-one guidance to students, helping them navigate their\n          educational journey with confidence and success. Hear from our Program Mentors Evaluators Our Evaluators help turn achievement into opportunity. As an Evaluator, you’ll use your expertise to assess student\n          work, provide meaningful feedback, and validate the competencies that move learners forward. If you’re driven by\n          quality, purpose, and helping students succeed, this is where your impact matters. Hear from our Evaluators Course Instructor Our Course Instructors bring learning to life at WGU. As a Course Instructor, you’ll have the opportunity to guide, coach, and inspire students as they build confidence, develop new skills, and progress toward their goals. Through meaningful connections and expert support, you’ll help turn potential into progress and make a lasting impact along the way. Hear from our Course Instructors Subject Matter Experts Our Subject Matter Experts (SMEs) help shape the learning experiences that power student success at WGU. As a recognized\n          expert in your field, you'll contribute as an independent contractor (1099), partnering with academic and learning\n          design teams on project-based work to create relevant, engaging course content that reflects current industry practices\n          and workforce needs. Through your expertise, you'll help ensure learners gain the knowledge and skills needed to achieve\n          their goals. View SME Opportunities Hear from Our People \"I absolutely love my role because it allows me to support students at some of the most pivotal moments in\n              their academic and professional journeys. As a Senior Program Mentor, my 'why' is rooted in helping\n              students build confidence, navigate challenges, and realize they are capable of far more than they\n              initially believed, just like my WGU Program Mentor did for me. This job feels like 'paying it forward'\n              and building meaningful connections all at the same time. Watching students overcome obstacles, persist\n              toward their goals, and grow throughout their program is what makes this work deeply meaningful to me.\" Lauren C., Sr. Program Mentor \"What I love most about my role is helping students realize that they can earn their education on their\n              own terms and that success is possible, even when life is complex. As a two-time WGU graduate, I bring\n              both lived experience and practical insight into my mentoring, using what I've learned to better support\n              students as they work toward their goals. What keeps me invested is WGU's innovative spirit and genuine\n              willingness to listen. Ideas are encouraged, growth is supported, and improving the student experience is\n              a shared responsibility. I've built a career here that I'm deeply proud of, and that pride shows up in the\n              care, consistency, and quality of support I provide to every student I serve.\" Wesley R., Sr. Program Mentor \"I've spent most of my life working in Education and Mental Health. As a Program Mentor, I get to use a\n              unique blend of both skillsets to help students navigate their academic, professional, and personal lives.\n              Each student's story is different; it's my role to truly listen, support, and meet each student where\n              they're at every single day.\" Ryan S., Program Mentor Get Answers and Take the Next Step Sage can answer questions, help you explore roles, and guide you through applying at WGU, right when you\n          need it. Chat now Open Jobs I'm Looking For Positions Near Use your location Search Search filters Filter Results Job Category Academic Community of Care 20 Administrative Community of Care 3 Program Development 6 City ALBUQUERQUE 1 Alexandria 1 Clinton 1 DALLAS 1 DAYTONA 1 EL PASO 2 Elko 2 FORT WAYNE 1 HOUSTON 3 State Florida 1 Indiana 2 Missouri 3 Nevada 3 New Mexico 1 Texas 6 Utah 12 Virginia 1 Clear Filter Showing 1 - 10 of 29 jobs Sort By Date Date Job Title Operations Manager Job Location Salt Lake City, UT Salt Lake City, UT Posting Date: 09/04/2026 JR-026097 FULL_TIME Apply Now Senior Strategist - Future of Education and AI Innovation Job Location Salt Lake City, UT Salt Lake City, UT Posting Date: 09/04/2026 JR-026100 FULL_TIME Apply Now Senior Psychometrician Job Location Salt Lake City, UT Salt Lake City, UT Posting Date: 09/03/2026 JR-025820 FULL_TIME Apply Now Full-Time Student Records Specialist - On-Site WGU Campus - Salt Lake City Location Job Location Salt Lake City, UT Salt Lake City, UT Posting Date: 09/03/2026 JR-026008 FULL_TIME Apply Now Onsite Instructor, Prelicensure Clinical - Houston, TX - Full Time Job Location HOUSTON, TX Houston, TX Posting Date: 09/03/2026 JR-025338 FULL_TIME Apply Now Onsite Instructor, Learning Lab - Indianapolis, IN - Part Time Job Location INDIANAPOLIS, IN Indianapolis, IN Posting Date: 09/03/2026 JR-026079 PART_TIME Apply Now Full-Time Instructor, Prelicensure (Multiple Specialty Opportunities) Job Location Salt Lake City, UT + 1 More Locations United States Remote Posting Date: 09/03/2026 JR-026090 FULL_TIME Apply Now Onsite Instructor, Prelicensure Clinical - Clinton, MO - Part Time Job Location Clinton, MO Clinton, MO Posting Date: 09/02/2026 JR-026071 PART_TIME Apply Now Lead Innovation Manager, Nursing and Health Job Location Salt Lake City, UT Salt Lake City, UT Posting Date: 09/02/2026 JR-025997 FULL_TIME Apply Now Full-Time Instructor, Prelicensure (Adult Health II & Critical Care) Job Location Salt Lake City, UT + 1 More Locations United States Remote Posting Date: 09/02/2026 JR-026069 FULL_TIME Apply Now Go to first page Go to previous page 1 2 3 Go to next page Go to last page 10 20 Explore Roles Academic Staff & Corporate Tech SME About WGU Life at WGU Benefits Where We Work Affiliates Visit wgu.edu Resources How We Hire Search Jobs Join Our Talent Community Privacy Policy | Cookie Policy | Contact Us © WGU. All rights reserved."
