    "https://jobs.wgu.edu/experience-solutions-designer/job/P1-6580034-0": {
      "title": "Experience Solutions Designer",
      "description": "Careers at WGU | Apply for Experience Solutions Designer Skip to content Jobs Search\n                All Jobs Academic\n                Careers Staff\n                & Corporate Careers Tech\n                Careers Schools School\n                of Technology School\n                of Business School\n                of Health School\n                of Education Life at WGU Life\n                at WGU Where\n                We Work Total\n                Rewards Search all jobs Close Site Navigation Careers Home Jobs Search All Jobs Academic Careers Staff & Corporate Careers Tech Careers Affiliates Schools School of Technology School of Business School of Health School of Education Life at WGU Where We Work Total Rewards How We Hire Talent Community (opens in new tab) Search all jobs Experience Solutions Designer Apply Now Chat to Apply Location Posted Date: End Date: Req ID: JR-026012 Share this Job 4001 South 700 East, Salt Lake City UT, United States Posting Date: 09/01/2026 Posting End Date: Loading... Loading... Job description If you’re passionate about building a better future for individuals, communities, and our country—and you’re committed to working hard to play your part in building that future—consider WGU as the next step in your career. Driven by a mission to expand access to higher education through online, competency-based degree programs, WGU is also committed to being a great place to work for a diverse workforce of student-focused professionals. The university has pioneered a new way to learn in the 21st century, one that has received praise from academic, industry, government, and media leaders. Whatever your role, working for WGU gives you a part to play in helping students graduate, creating a better tomorrow for themselves and their families. Pay Range: $75,200.00 - $112,700.00 Essential Functions and Responsibilities: Plan and manage medium-scale university-level projects impacting segments of faculty, students and operations across departments. Determine organizational readiness and develop project schedules by analyzing organizational assets, enterprise environmental factors, task dependencies, resource requirements, work breakdown, and departmental strategy and priorities. Leverage system-thinking approach when presenting to college leadership and primary stakeholders to influence decision making, gain buy-in and support for systemic change that improve faculty engagement and student outcomes. Responsible for planning, organizing, monitoring, and documenting all phases of projects. Analyze current state business processes and identify improvement opportunities in policies, business processes, services, and service level agreements. Collaborate with cross-functional leadership to develop key features of faculty engagement and student-centric models, including modular support/employment models and continuous improvement processes. Develop and deliver project and solutions updates, communications, and reports used to drive priorities and allocation of resources across WGU departments. Develop and maintain professional working relations and communication with stakeholders, project team members, departments, and outside contacts. Ensure projects meet organizational standards and are managed in accordance with applicable policies, processes, and procedures Documents project deliverables, outputs, and notes that capture why key project decisions were made Assess project impact faculty and student experience and outcomes. Deliver financial and quality commitments according to the strategic plan. Performs other related duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skill and Abilities: Demonstrated strong verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to interact and tailor messages effectively with people at all levels of the organization. Deep analytical knowledge in interpreting multifaceted problems and complex data to meet business goals and objectives. Strong critical thinking and problem-solving skills while working within a collaborative matrix organization. Systems thinker who can identify systemic structures contributing to outcomes, identify high leverage activities to impact outcomes, and articulate the implications of business decisions Proficiency in project management, change management, data analytics Excellent presentation and communication skills to a broad audience across multiple departments and stakeholders with a technical writing emphasis Ability to develop a business case and models Highly organized and detail orientated Proven ability to take initiative and be both innovative and flexible Experience leading teams and works well in a team environment Strong technical and problem-solving skills. Ability to plan and meet schedules for both individual and collaborative projects. Ability to create concise, informative reports on projects and initiatives Ability to clearly document and catalog information and progress on assigned projects Proficiency with Office 365 applications, live event tools, CRM software, data visualization applications Design-thinking and documented use of technology-based educational delivery systems Ability to understand current/changing business processes, participation in defining application and platform functionality. Ability to build consensus and motivate others. Competencies: Works to achieve operational targets within job areas impacting department, function, or office results.​ Work is performed independently on moderately complex projects and assignments with some guidance required for direction and complex tasks. Sets objectives for oneself to meet the goals of projects or assignments.​ Problem Solving & Decision Making: Responsible for employing adjustments or recommended enhancements to systems and processes to solve problems or improve the job area's effectiveness while leveraging a systems-thinking approach.​ Problems faced may require an understanding of a broader set of issues and job areas. Communication & Influence: Collaborates with contacts typically within the job area to obtain or provide information requiring some explanation or interpretation. Systems-thinking approach Leadership & Talent Management May provide guidance and assistance to entry-level professionals and or support employees.​ Demonstrates the WGU leadership principles in all aspects of service to students, employees, and partners of WGU. Job Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in a related field from an accredited college or university. Education is verified Two (2) years of related experience in a role that required extensive project and change management skills in a large and distributed organization Direct experience testing, developing, implementing, and measuring the impact of technology or business processes Preferred Qualifications: Masters degree from an accredited college or university Five years of experience as the assigned project manager of executive-sponsored projects, with sole responsibility for project initiation, planning, execution, monitoring, and closure Three years of experience in higher education and competency-based education Demonstrated experience managing teams and initiatives to impact student outcomes through specific interventions Experience in supervising and leading people Demonstrated professional experience in communication to a broad audience base, with a technical writing emphasis Demonstrated professional experience managing complex projects and working cross-functionally Proficient in project management software tools and collaboration software Physical Requirements: Prolonged periods sitting at a desk and working on a computer Must be able to lift 15 pounds at times This position requires occasional travel of up to 20%, including required attendance at designated company summits (typically one to two per year). Additional travel may include conferences, visits to company locations, and other business-related events as needed. Additional travel may be assigned as needed to support business requirements. #LI-HS1 #AA Additional Information Full-Time Regular Positions (classified as regular and working 40 standard weekly hours): This is a full-time, regular position (classified for 40 standard weekly hours) that is eligible for bonuses; medical, dental, vision, telehealth and mental healthcare; health savings account and flexible spending account; basic and voluntary life insurance; disability coverage; accident, critical illness and hospital indemnity supplemental coverages; legal and identity theft coverage; retirement savings plan; wellbeing program; discounted WGU tuition; and flexible paid time off for rest and relaxation with no need for accrual, flexible paid sick time with no need for accrual, 11 paid holidays, and other paid leaves, including up to 12 weeks of parental leave. Disclaimer: The job posting highlights the most critical responsibilities and requirements of the job. It’s not all-inclusive. Accommodations: Applicants with disabilities who require assistance or accommodation during the application or interview process should contact our Talent Acquisition team at recruiting@wgu.edu . Equal Employment Opportunity: All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to any protected characteristic as required by law. Apply Now Chat to Apply Location Explore Roles Academic Staff & Corporate Tech SME About WGU Life at WGU Benefits Where We Work Affiliates Visit wgu.edu Resources How We Hire Search Jobs Join Our Talent Community Privacy Policy | Cookie Policy | Contact Us © WGU. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://jobs.wgu.edu/academic-careers/page/1": {
      "title": "Academic Careers",
      "description": "Academic & Faculty Careers | WGU Skip to content Jobs Search\n                All Jobs Academic\n                Careers Staff\n                & Corporate Careers Tech\n                Careers Schools School\n                of Technology School\n                of Business School\n                of Health School\n                of Education Life at WGU Life\n                at WGU Where\n                We Work Total\n                Rewards Search all jobs Close Site Navigation Careers Home Jobs Search All Jobs Academic Careers Staff & Corporate Careers Tech Careers Affiliates Schools School of Technology School of Business School of Health School of Education Life at WGU Where We Work Total Rewards How We Hire Talent Community (opens in new tab) Search all jobs Academic Careers Educate. Motivate. Transform. Academic careers at WGU focus on supporting learners through mentorship, instruction, and meaningful assessment.\n        As a faculty member or academic leader, you’ll help learners build real-world skills, stay on track, and move\n        confidently toward their goals. Find a Teaching Role That Matches Your Passion for Education Academic Career Paths Faculty Faculty roles at WGU are about making a direct, meaningful difference in learners' lives. You'll serve\n                  as a Mentor, Instructor, or Evaluator, providing personalized support, coaching, and instruction that\n                  helps learners progress with confidence in a flexible, competency-based environment. Accreditation & Compliance Accreditation and Compliance roles support the foundation that makes everything else possible. You'll\n                  help ensure academic quality, integrity, and trust—working behind the scenes to meet regulatory\n                  standards while enabling innovation and a continuous improvement model. Academic Strategy Academic Strategy roles are ideal for big-picture thinkers who enjoy turning insight into action.\n                  You'll work at the intersection of data, innovation, and academic excellence—helping WGU design,\n                  launch, and evolve programs that meet the needs of today's learners and tomorrow's workforce. Academic Leadership Academic Leadership roles are for those who want to lead with purpose and shape the future of\n                  education. In this area, you'll guide academic teams, influence strategy, and help scale innovative\n                  learning models that expand access and improve learner outcomes. Program Development & Learning Design Program Development and Learning Design roles are for creators and problem-solvers who want to build\n                  impactful learning experiences. In this area, you'll collaborate with academic and industry partners\n                  to design modern, engaging programs that prepare learners for real-world success. Program Mentor Our Program Mentors are the heart of our student success model at WGU. As a Program Mentor, you'll have the\n          unique opportunity to provide personalized, one-on-one guidance to students, helping them navigate their\n          educational journey with confidence and success. Hear from our Program Mentors Evaluators Our Evaluators help turn achievement into opportunity. As an Evaluator, you’ll use your expertise to assess student\n          work, provide meaningful feedback, and validate the competencies that move learners forward. If you’re driven by\n          quality, purpose, and helping students succeed, this is where your impact matters. Hear from our Evaluators Course Instructor Our Course Instructors bring learning to life at WGU. As a Course Instructor, you’ll have the opportunity to guide, coach, and inspire students as they build confidence, develop new skills, and progress toward their goals. Through meaningful connections and expert support, you’ll help turn potential into progress and make a lasting impact along the way. Hear from our Course Instructors Subject Matter Experts Our Subject Matter Experts (SMEs) help shape the learning experiences that power student success at WGU. As a recognized\n          expert in your field, you'll contribute as an independent contractor (1099), partnering with academic and learning\n          design teams on project-based work to create relevant, engaging course content that reflects current industry practices\n          and workforce needs. Through your expertise, you'll help ensure learners gain the knowledge and skills needed to achieve\n          their goals. View SME Opportunities Hear from Our People \"I absolutely love my role because it allows me to support students at some of the most pivotal moments in\n              their academic and professional journeys. As a Senior Program Mentor, my 'why' is rooted in helping\n              students build confidence, navigate challenges, and realize they are capable of far more than they\n              initially believed, just like my WGU Program Mentor did for me. This job feels like 'paying it forward'\n              and building meaningful connections all at the same time. Watching students overcome obstacles, persist\n              toward their goals, and grow throughout their program is what makes this work deeply meaningful to me.\" Lauren C., Sr. Program Mentor \"What I love most about my role is helping students realize that they can earn their education on their\n              own terms and that success is possible, even when life is complex. As a two-time WGU graduate, I bring\n              both lived experience and practical insight into my mentoring, using what I've learned to better support\n              students as they work toward their goals. What keeps me invested is WGU's innovative spirit and genuine\n              willingness to listen. Ideas are encouraged, growth is supported, and improving the student experience is\n              a shared responsibility. I've built a career here that I'm deeply proud of, and that pride shows up in the\n              care, consistency, and quality of support I provide to every student I serve.\" Wesley R., Sr. Program Mentor \"I've spent most of my life working in Education and Mental Health. As a Program Mentor, I get to use a\n              unique blend of both skillsets to help students navigate their academic, professional, and personal lives.\n              Each student's story is different; it's my role to truly listen, support, and meet each student where\n              they're at every single day.\" Ryan S., Program Mentor Get Answers and Take the Next Step Sage can answer questions, help you explore roles, and guide you through applying at WGU, right when you\n          need it. Chat now Open Jobs I'm Looking For Positions Near Use your location Search Search filters Filter Results Job Category Academic Community of Care 20 Administrative Community of Care 3 Program Development 6 City ALBUQUERQUE 1 Alexandria 1 Clinton 1 DALLAS 1 DAYTONA 1 EL PASO 2 Elko 2 FORT WAYNE 1 HOUSTON 3 State Florida 1 Indiana 2 Missouri 3 Nevada 3 New Mexico 1 Texas 6 Utah 12 Virginia 1 Clear Filter Showing 1 - 10 of 29 jobs Sort By Date Date Job Title Operations Manager Job Location Salt Lake City, UT Salt Lake City, UT Posting Date: 09/04/2026 JR-026097 FULL_TIME Apply Now Senior Strategist - Future of Education and AI Innovation Job Location Salt Lake City, UT Salt Lake City, UT Posting Date: 09/04/2026 JR-026100 FULL_TIME Apply Now Senior Psychometrician Job Location Salt Lake City, UT Salt Lake City, UT Posting Date: 09/03/2026 JR-025820 FULL_TIME Apply Now Full-Time Student Records Specialist - On-Site WGU Campus - Salt Lake City Location Job Location Salt Lake City, UT Salt Lake City, UT Posting Date: 09/03/2026 JR-026008 FULL_TIME Apply Now Onsite Instructor, Prelicensure Clinical - Houston, TX - Full Time Job Location HOUSTON, TX Houston, TX Posting Date: 09/03/2026 JR-025338 FULL_TIME Apply Now Onsite Instructor, Learning Lab - Indianapolis, IN - Part Time Job Location INDIANAPOLIS, IN Indianapolis, IN Posting Date: 09/03/2026 JR-026079 PART_TIME Apply Now Full-Time Instructor, Prelicensure (Multiple Specialty Opportunities) Job Location Salt Lake City, UT + 1 More Locations United States Remote Posting Date: 09/03/2026 JR-026090 FULL_TIME Apply Now Onsite Instructor, Prelicensure Clinical - Clinton, MO - Part Time Job Location Clinton, MO Clinton, MO Posting Date: 09/02/2026 JR-026071 PART_TIME Apply Now Lead Innovation Manager, Nursing and Health Job Location Salt Lake City, UT Salt Lake City, UT Posting Date: 09/02/2026 JR-025997 FULL_TIME Apply Now Full-Time Instructor, Prelicensure (Adult Health II & Critical Care) Job Location Salt Lake City, UT + 1 More Locations United States Remote Posting Date: 09/02/2026 JR-026069 FULL_TIME Apply Now Go to first page Go to previous page 1 2 3 Go to next page Go to last page 10 20 Explore Roles Academic Staff & Corporate Tech SME About WGU Life at WGU Benefits Where We Work Affiliates Visit wgu.edu Resources How We Hire Search Jobs Join Our Talent Community Privacy Policy | Cookie Policy | Contact Us © WGU. All rights reserved."
    },
